<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Nearer, My God, to Thee (Carl Nielsen)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">paraphrase of the tune for wind band</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">In Memoriam – Titanic (Joseph Bonnet)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1913</span><span class="sg-chain-h">organ piece on the tune &quot;Horbury&quot;, the first of his Douze Pièces, Op. 10</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 4 (Charles Ives)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quotes the tune &quot;Bethany&quot;</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Plus près de toi, mon Dieu</span><span class="sg-chain-h">French version, sung in Max Ophüls's film Le Plaisir (1952)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Nearer, My God: An Autobiography of Faith (William F. Buckley)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1998</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title taken from the hymn</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Genesis 28:11–12 (Jacob's dream)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the story it retells</span></li></ul></section>
